@*
    The note over the view while something loads: what is loading, and Cancel. The shell says what and does the
    cancel - see its loadingWhat and cancelLoad.

    Its own component so that it can be drawn again on its own as a load's file goes in, when the stage it shows
    changes and nothing renders the page around it until the view arriving has drawn - the 3D view's merge is seconds
    of a real chip, which the note spent saying the file was still being read. Rendering the page itself there is not
    the same thing: it runs what follows a render of the page - a restored session's settings, a link's - into the
    middle of the load, ahead of the draw they are meant to land after. See Refresh.
*@
@if (What.Length > 0)
{
    @*
        data-stage says whether the file has gone in yet - reading until it has, drawing after - which is the
        difference between what a cancel has to put back. See the shell's cancelLoad.

        The status is the message alone, so what is read out is what is loading rather than that and the name of the
        button beside it.
    *@
    <div id="viewLoading" class="viewLoading" data-stage="@stage()">
        <span class="viewLoadingSpinner" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span role="status" aria-live="polite">@What&hellip;</span>

        @if (Cancelable)
        {
            <button type="button" id="cancelLoad" class="viewLoadingCancel" @onclick="OnCancel"
                    title="Stop loading, and go back to what was on screen">
                Cancel
            </button>
        }
    </div>
}

@code {
    ///<summary>What is loading, as the note says it - or empty, for no note.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string What { get; set; } = "";

    ///<summary>Whether the load offers Cancel, which the way back from one does not - see Pacer.CanCancel.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public bool Cancelable { get; set; }

    ///
    ///Asks whether the load's file has gone in yet. Asked rather than handed over, because a value is only as new as
    ///the page's last render, and Refresh draws the note without one.
    ///
    [Parameter]
    public Func<bool>? FileIn { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback OnCancel { get; set; }

    ///<summary>Draws the note again, and nothing else on the page: for a load whose file has just gone in.</summary>
    public void Refresh()
    {
        StateHasChanged();
    }

    private string stage()
    {
        if (FileIn is not null && FileIn())
            return "drawing";

        return "reading";
    }
}
